  "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡({x}^{2}-1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{({x}^{2}-1)}^{2}}\\cdot {({x}^{2}-1)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-({x}^{4}-2{x}^{2}+1)}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{2{x}^{2}-{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}(2-{x}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x(2-{x}^{2})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
